page('about.html','About', '''<div class="intro"><p class="eyebrow">About David Stroupe</p><h1>Operational experience.<br>A focus on the person using the tool.</h1><p class="lead">I bring more than 20 years of Department of Defense experience to data visualization, reporting, and operational applications.</p></div><div class="text-page"><p>My career began in the U.S. Navy, working across personnel programs, administration, and career counseling. That work taught me to turn complicated requirements into information people can act on.</p><p>Today, I build operational dashboards and analytical tools at Leidos. I review incoming requests, assess the available data, and develop applications in Palantir Foundry Workshop. My earlier work includes Power BI reporting, Power Automate pipelines, and SharePoint portals.</p><h2>What guides my work</h2><p>Moving a process onto a new screen is only worth doing if it makes the work easier. I look at what users need, what information is available, and where the experience can improve.</p><h2>Developing my design practice</h2><p>I am enrolled in the Google UX Design certificate course and developing my skills in Figma. My first independent project, Operations Overview, brings together editable Figma layouts, a working dashboard, and notes about the design decisions. My course portfolio projects will be added as I complete them.</p><h2>Experience</h2><p>Leidos · Addx Corporation · FedWriters · Booz Allen Hamilton · WWC Federal / WWC Global · United States Navy</p><p>My background spans operational dashboards, executive reporting, knowledge management, SharePoint administration, and personnel operations.</p><p class="note">This portfolio uses generic descriptions and original illustrations. It contains no customer screenshots, operational datasets, or program specific details.</p></div>''','David Stroupe is a U.S. Navy veteran and data visualization analyst with more than 20 years of DoD experience.')
page('accessibility.html','Accessibility', '''<div class="intro"><p class="eyebrow">Accessibility</p><h1>Designed to be usable.</h1></div><div class="text-page"><p>This site uses semantic page structure, visible keyboard focus, a skip link, descriptive links, responsive layouts, and reduced motion preferences. Information is presented in text rather than relying only on visuals or color.</p><p>I have checked the basics, but there is more to test. The target is WCAG 2.2 AA, but this site has not had a full conformance assessment or a formal Section 508 review. <a href="https://github.com/dnstroupe/data-design-portfolio/blob/main/ACCESSIBILITY.md">The accessibility notes</a> record the checks and remaining work.</p><p>If you encounter a barrier, please contact me through LinkedIn and describe the page and the difficulty.</p></div>''','Accessibility information for David Stroupe’s portfolio.')
